From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: max77705: open the USB-C opcode response window

The USB-C block answers its opcodes at 0x51 with up to 32 data bytes.
Extend the regmap to 0x71 so the charger can read the answers.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
--- a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
@@ -105,7 +105,8 @@ static const struct regmap_irq_chip max77705_irq_chip = {
 static const struct regmap_config max77705_usbc_regmap_config = {
 	.reg_bits = 8,
 	.val_bits = 8,
-	.max_register = MAX77705_USBC_OPCODE_WRITE_END,
+	/* the opcode response window, 0x51 and 32 data bytes */
+	.max_register = 0x71,
 };
 
 /*
